# GATE 4's module probe on a mean-expression metric, by arithmetic (read after R1's result)
# metric: mean over cells of log1p(CP10k of the marker); delta_min 0.25 (0.5 x SESOI 0.5)

## 1. The identity: response over all cells = share of cells with the marker x response in them
  B2 (b2_sex_structure.log): 0.2581 x +0.6310 = +0.1629; measured over all cells +0.1627 (separate runs, so equal up to their Monte Carlo error)

## 2. The bound for a well-detected marker: frac x share x ln 2
  ln 2 = 0.6931; f(2x) - f(x) = ln((1 + 2x)/(1 + x)) < ln 2 for every x, e.g. x = 6: 0.6190, x = 50: 0.6833
  the default (frac 0.3) with the marker in every cell: at most 0.2079, below delta_min 0.25: it cannot pass
  R1's probe (frac 1) needs a share of at least 0.25 / ln 2 = 0.3607 of cells with the marker; B2 has 0.2581: the failure follows from B2's composition and anchors.py's constants
  with B2's measured response in its Xist cells (+0.6310, below ln 2: Xist is well detected there), the share needed is 0.25 / 0.6310 = 0.3962
  at depth 20,000, marker at CP10k 50: frac 0.3 x ln((1 + 2x)/(1 + x)) = 0.2050; simulated +0.2050 (frac 1.0: 0.6833; simulated +0.6831)
  at depth 20,000, marker at CP10k 6: frac 0.3 x ln((1 + 2x)/(1 + x)) = 0.1857; simulated +0.1956 (frac 1.0: 0.6190; simulated +0.6517)
  where the simulation exceeds the formula, the excess is the sham's thinning of the marker's counts, which the formula leaves out

## 3. One count of the marker in a cell of depth 2,000
  untouched: CP10k 4.998, f 1.7913
  injected (other genes halved): CP10k 9.990, f 2.3970; the 2-fold change adds 0.6056
  sham (every gene halved): f 1.1985 on average; the sham's loss of the single count adds 0.5928
  frac 1: response 1 x (0.6056 + 0.5928) = 1.1985, of which the 2-fold change 0.6056 and the sham's loss 0.5928
  frac 0.3: response 0.3 x (0.6056 + 0.5928) = 0.3595, of which the 2-fold change 0.1817 and the sham's loss 0.1779
  simulated (gate4_module_dilution.log, depth about 2,000, a marker of one count): frac 0.3 +0.3580, frac 1.0 +1.2022
  so the default passes there only through the sham: the 2-fold change alone gives 0.1817, below delta_min 0.25
  and the response in the marker's cells (frac 1) is 1.1985, above ln 2 = 0.6931: the bound of section 2 does not hold for a marker of single counts
